cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "The Ledger Test: Can Reliability Scores Improve — or Corrupt — AI Forecast Aggregation?"
authors:
  - family-names: Bhatia
    given-names: Harsh
date-released: 2026-11-15
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/harshb16/ledger-test"
abstract: >-
  Tests whether showing LLM aggregators each forecaster's track record improves their
  aggregate forecasts, how much the models rely on those records, and whether the records
  can be gamed by padding. Uses ForecastBench human-round data, four LLMs and
  pre-registered confirmatory tests.
keywords:
  - forecast aggregation
  - track records
  - LLM evaluation
  - reputation farming
  - epistemics
